 # Changelog
 
+## 1.6.0
+
+- Ticket assignment. `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee` assigns an open or in-progress ticket to an agent (`{"assignee": "sam"}`) or
+  unassigns it (`{"assignee": null}`); the agent is notified (`ticket.assigned`). Every ticket shows its `assignee`, null when
+  unassigned, and `GET /tickets?assignee=sam` (or `assignee=` for the unassigned) filters on it.
+- Filters of `GET /tickets` now combine as documented: a ticket must match every filter given (it used to be listed when it
+  matched any one of them).
+- The command line shows the assignee: an ASSIGNEE column in `list`, a fifth column in `list --raw` (the first four keep their
+  places), and `list --assignee AGENT`.
+- The data file keeps `assignee` on assigned tickets only, so the format is still version 1 and 1.5.0 and 1.4.0 ignore it.
+
 ## 1.5.0
 
 - Due times ([decision 9](docs/decisions/0009-due-times.md)). Every ticket gets a due time, `due`: the time it was created
