+### Assign a ticket: `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee`
+
+```json
+{ "assignee": "sam" }
+```
+
+Assigns the ticket to the agent, a non-empty name of at most 64 characters (surrounding spaces are dropped); `{ "assignee": null }`
+unassigns it. Answers 200 with the ticket. Only `open` and `in_progress` tickets can be assigned or unassigned: for a
+`resolved` or `closed` one the answer is 409 `conflict`. A body without `assignee`, or with any other field, or a name that
+is empty, too long or not a string is 400 `invalid`. Assigning the agent the ticket already has (or unassigning an
+unassigned ticket) changes nothing: no audit entry, no notification, and `updated` stays. When a ticket is assigned, the agent
+is notified; unassigning notifies no one.
+
